[Music]  many fans cannot wait until they can  finally watch the upcoming venom let  there be carnage in theaters  we feel the same obviously and in order  to make the waiting time a bit easier  for you  we prepared an original episode for you  this week learn everything you need to  know about the new sony blockbuster  as well as the latest news in regards to  cast story and production  let's start with the storyline first  after the first film was released in  2018 fans were thrilled to bits and  notches due to the gripping and chaotic  story around eddie block aka venom  in particular one mid credit scene of  the film with tom hardy is significant  for part two  anyone who has seen venom will know  exactly what we mean we're talking about  the scene in which protagonist eddie  brock encounters serial killer cletus  cassidy aka carnage  in a maximum security prison cassidy  like brock is also the host of the  symbiote whose nature is at least as  terrifying as venoms in the mid-credit  scene cassidy who is played by woody  harrelson  announces that he is going to break out  of prison using the memorable words  let there be carnage at the latest from  this scene it was clear that a second  part was to come  not much is known about the plot but at  least you can get a rough idea from  venom let there be carnage based on some  leaked information  the first part ends spectacularly with  the explosion of the spaceship and the  death of eddie brock's nemesis dr carter  drake a.k.a right  as deadline also reported comic book  villain shriek will be assisting  antagonist carnage shriek whose real  name is  francis barrison is a drug dealer in the  comics who obtains her mutant powers due  to a  severe trauma her [ __ ] of superpowers  includes flying evoking traumatic  emotions in her opponent and the control  of  sound waves the latter should be  especially tough on venom  as he's known to be very sensitive to  frequency interference  another juicy detail from the comics is  that she is both carnage's accomplice  and his lover so her appearance is  considered to be  very likely despite the lack of  confirmation from sony's part  quite surprisingly a first almost two  minute trailer came out which gives a  first glimpse of the movie  eddie brock seems to have come to terms  with his dark side by now  and experiences some pretty funny upbeat  very absurd moments in everyday life  but not everything is as nice as it  seems at first glance as of course the  title  antagonist carnage also makes an  appearance in the first trailer  in one brutal scene for instance we can  witness cletus cassie transforming into  the terrified carnage  at the moment of his execution naomi  harris who will be playing the  aforementioned shriek in the upcoming  film is also featured all in all  an exciting first trailer that leaves  you wanting to see more  so now let's move on to the cast in  front of and behind the camera  the cast confirmed so far is of course  tom hardy is venom naomi here is a  shriek and woody harrelson has carnage  other confirmed cast members include  michelle williams's anne wieng and reed  scott as dr dan lewis  behind the scenes andy circus is  responsible for directing the  blockbuster  in 2019 brit took over the role from  ruben fleischer  as he was too busy producing zombieland  doubletap and lag time for venom 2.  the screenplay was originally written by  kelly marcel  but lead actor tom hardy was also very  much involved in the writing process  now let's take a look at the third  aspect the rumor mill surrounding venom  2  the rumor that spider-man will appear  more or less directly in the upcoming  sony film has been persistent for some  time  conveniently director andy circus has  analyzed the new trailer in a video from  ign  and revealed some bits of information  the 57 year old  acknowledges a certain connection  between spider-man and venom but at the  same time stresses that it was decided  to  isolate the venom universe from the  superhero therefore venom and carnage  do not know about peter parker's  existence still  that doesn't mean that clever fans won't  find a few easter eggs in this regard  venom let there be carnage does contain  some illusions  for example peter parker's employer the  daily bugle will also appear in the new  venom movie  since sony's new multiverse doesn't  really start until venom 2  we can most likely expect to see  spider-man in the upcoming blockbusters  surrounding morbius  craven the hunter the sinister 6 or  madame web  another connection to the mcu can also  be found in the new trailer  in one scene you can see an unfamiliar  man browsing through the daily bugle  if you slow down the video and pause at  the right moment you can see a headline  about the avengers on the right hand  side as seen from his perspective  sadly the text is only partially visible  and really cleverly hidden  but this is certainly not just a  coincidence the trailer also reveals an  interesting film location in the  beautiful panoramic view  the ravencroft institute to put it  crudely it's the arkham asylum of the  marvel universe and just like the dc  model  not all inmates leave the institute as  reformed criminals  specifically in vellum 2 ravencroft will  primarily act as the focus of various  scientific experiments most of which  will certainly revolve around  symbiotes and their hosts there are also  some indications that venom will set the  institute on fire during the course of  the film  you can tell it's going to be exciting  another easter egg revolves around none  other than spider-man  well at least a spider and the man in  the scene you can  see an unknown figure killing a spider  with his hand you don't have to be a pro  to recognize that is pretty much  carnage himself as can be seen by his  blue jumpsuit after all  obviously it's clear to everyone which  imagery this clip wants to convey and we  sincerely hope that this is a small  teaser of a big clash between cassidy  and peter parker  even though it's not going to happen in  this movie needless to say there are  many more easter eggs and clues to be  discovered so we'd be interested to hear  which ones you've spotted post them down  in the comments if you like  last but not least we want to introduce  you to the titular antagonist carnage  casually speaking carnage is the truly  evil one among spider-man's enemies  for while most of the adversaries have  experienced tragic events in their way  to become  villains and still possess some spark of  humanity it is simply a carnage's nature  to kill and destroy  before cletus cassidy was infected with  the symbiote carnage he was already a  criminal sadist this is certainly  one of the reasons why carnage is one of  the most difficult adversaries  simply because once he gets into fury  he's nearly unstoppable  if you will carnage is the nastier and  stronger version of venom as can be seen  quite well in this similarly designed  custom of the two the scope of the  superpowers is also impressive  as they include not only supernatural  strength agility and speed but also the  ability to block the popular superhero  spider-sense  moreover a currency symbiote grew on  earth rather than on the planet clina  which does make him more unstable and  unpredictable but also considerably  stronger than the main character venom  his greatest vulnerability is fire but  in exchange he is not as  acceptable to sonic weapons as his  counterpart all in all a very powerful  villain who will give protagonist eddie  brock some real trouble  that's it for our latest original  episode are you excited about venom let  there be carnage as we are and what are  your expectations of the new sony  blockbuster  let's chat in the comments if you also  enjoyed the video like and subscribe so  we can give you more insights into your  favorite movies in the future  see you next time  [Music]  you

